hey everyone its Johanna here one of the  most common questions I received is how  do I get rid of my belly fat well I came  across this article in ideas fitness  journal which basically explains the  methods behind getting rid of that  stubborn belly fat it is a very detailed  article and so I am going to try my best  to provide you with as much information  as possible  so let's first start by understanding  what makes our belly fat there are three  layers to recognize first visceral belly  fat which is also known as the deep fat  this lies around the organs under the  abdominal muscles and can't be pinched  second superficial subcutaneous belly  fat which hangs over the waistline and  this can be pinched third deep  subcutaneous belly fat a hybrid of both  in this video we will be focusing on the  first two fats let's get to know them  the visceral belly fat is rich in beta  receptors it has high blood supply and  it is easier to burn the superficial  subcutaneous belly fat is rich in alpha  receptors has lower blood supply and it  is harder to burn this is the fat most  of us are concerned about because we can  visually see it hanging over our waste  line there are two enzymes which are  responsible for holding on to fat and  also burning it they are first  lipoprotein lipase LPL this enzyme is  responsible for fat storage second  hormone sensitive lipase HSL this enzyme  is involved in fat release which is what  we want so to be valid that it is not  just about creating calorie deficit it  is a combination of calorie deficit with  hormone balance the main hormones that  impact LPL activity are your insulin and  your cortisol so to simply put insulin  cortisol equals belly fat bullies the  hottest insulin causes belly fat when it  comes to the brain muscles and liver you  want the body to be insulin sensitive  and not resistance being insulin  resistance in these areas make a person  unable to burn fat and sugar or to feel  satisfied after eating this is why many  overweight people who are instantly  resistant in these tissues tend to  overeat because they are hungry all the  time  how does cortisol causes belly fat well  excess cortisol in our body can drive us  to eat more of the wrong foods more  often which means higher daily calorie  intake and fat gain this also causes  small immature fat cells to become  larger matured fat cells which is not a  good thing  when you are trying to burn belly fat in  order to burn fat we want to make sure  that these hormones are well balanced in  our body let's just start by making it  clear that diets don't work  dieting makes belly fat fatter the  common eat less exercise more approach  it's only a short-term success  this approach accomplishes the calorie  deficit but makes the hormone balance  worse  remember to burn belly fat equals  calorie deficit plus balance hormones  just think of insulin as a starch and  sugar hormone and cortisol as a sleep  and stress hormone I am sure you have  heard about the low carb and high  protein approach to reduce belly fat  this would work however a diet too low  in carbs which can cause low blood sugar  stresses of the body and raises cortisol  levels hence you do not want a diet too  low in carbs instead choosing the right  cups which are lower in glycemic load  can help with benefits and also to  reduce weight gain overall to apply this  think of a combination of protein and  vegetables as they help to suppress  hunger with minimal insulin production  this results in fewer calories consumed  and a good hormone balance please visit  the  link below for a comprehensive list of  glycemic load in foods as for dealing  with the cortisol hormone sleep and  stress management is essential in for a  good seven to eight hours of sleep every  night and practicing medication upcoming  exercises will help as well you need to  give time back to yourself mentally and  physically so to sum up when dealing  with visceral belly fat the deep fat  which has better blood flow and easier  to burn exercising stress management and  reducing cups in moderation will help it  is important to know that even if your  thing you can still have too much  visceral fat this comes down to your  genes and your lifestyle especially how  active you are visceral that likes  inactivity even if you do watch over  your diet and maintain a sleep figure  but do not exercise you are more likely  to have too much a visceral fat and this  can cause serious health problems the  key is to be active no matter what size  you are when it comes to building  subcutaneous belly fat the love handles  fat which is the subtle fat as it has  lower blood flow exercising on its own  it's not enough  reducing cops intake to low level is  usually the major focus when addressing  this matter hence the low carbs high  protein model would work so how or what  should you eat we have spoken about how  the traditional method of eat less  exercise more won't work there are two  methods to burn belly fat first it last  exercise less approach second eat more  exercise more approach both these  methods generate low calorie intake and  naturally reduce starch intake in a way  that provides enough fill to keep hunger  energy and cravings stable but not  enough to slow fat loss for the eat less  exercise less approach let's take a look  at the three to one plan 3 stands for  three meals per day two means two of  those meals should be mostly protein and  fiber with  as starch 1 means 1 mill in a day should  have heavier starch this meal is best  consumed as your post-workout meal to  visualize this on a plate three parts  should be vegetables two parts protein  and one part starch you can also think  of this in terms of bytes for every  three bites of vegetables you have two  bytes of protein and one byte of starch  this three-two-one approach works well  for those of you who are not heavy  exercises I would say if you train three  times or less in a week or you perform  gentle 